Everyone has to play the early game, but there are two ways to finish
the game. One is to use your God-given wits and ingenuity, plus
whatever meagre supplies you have been able to amass, to dodge through
all the hazards and win through to the High Altar on your last WoD
charge. We will call this Good Ol'Fashioned All-American Nethack. The
other is to spend a certain amount of planning and effort to set up a
scriptable environment, get piles of loot, and then steamroller
through the endgame flattening everything in sight. Obviously this is
Godless-Socialist Corrupt Nethack. So let there be a fork: FarmHack
for the decadent bourgeoisie and FarmlessHack for the upstanding sons
of the soil.

Setting aside the score issue and the public server issue for a
moment, let us consider those who play only on their own computers. If
you don't enjoy the latter half of the game, and there is a option to
bypass it, or you get a kick out of being a steamroller, and there is
an option to permit it, why is it *wrong* to do so?

